test.yaml:7:14: "npm install" resolves the dependencies again and may update the package-lock.json instead of failing when it is out of date. use `npm ci` [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:8:14: "npm i" resolves the dependencies again and may update the package-lock.json instead of failing when it is out of date. use `npm ci` [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:9:14: "yarn" does not require the yarn.lock to be up to date in Yarn 1, and relies on the CI detection of Yarn 2+. pass `--immutable` (`--frozen-lockfile` for Yarn 1) [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:10:14: "yarn install" does not require the yarn.lock to be up to date in Yarn 1, and relies on the CI detection of Yarn 2+. pass `--immutable` (`--frozen-lockfile` for Yarn 1) [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:11:14: "bun install" may update bun.lock instead of failing when it is out of date. use `bun ci` or pass `--frozen-lockfile` [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:12:14: "pnpm install" is told not to freeze the lock file, so it may update pnpm-lock.yaml instead of failing when it is out of date. pass --frozen-lockfile [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:13:14: "pnpm install" is told not to freeze the lock file, so it may update pnpm-lock.yaml instead of failing when it is out of date. pass --frozen-lockfile [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:14:14: "pip install -r requirements.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:15:14: "pip3 install -r requirements/dev.txt -r requirements/test.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:16:14: "uv pip install -r requirements.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install-pedantic]
test.yaml:17:14: "python -m pip install -r requirements.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install-pedantic]
